(55, 0, 'No3', '<p><span id=\"tg_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">DHCP server is configured on a router\'s ether1 interface. IP address 192.168.0.100/24 is assigned to </span><span id=\"th_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">the interface. Possible IP pools, that can be used by this DHCP server, are:</span></p>', 1, '', 1, 100.0000000, 0.0000000, 'multichoice', 1, '192.168.19.27+260422071108+wgpVPG', 1776841868, 1776841868, 2, 2),
(56, 0, 'No3', '<p><span id=\"tg_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">DHCP server is configured on a router\'s ether1 interface. IP address 192.168.0.100/24 is assigned to </span><span id=\"th_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">the interface. Possible IP pools, that can be used by this DHCP server, are:</span></p>', 1, '', 1, 1.0000000, 0.0000000, 'multichoice', 1, '192.168.19.27+260422071631+azuE9a', 1776842191, 1776842191, 2, 2),
(57, 0, 'No4', '<p><span id=\"tq_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">You have a DHCP server on your MikroTik router. The IP addresses 10.1.2.2-10.2.2.20 are distributed in </span><span id=\"tr_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">the DHCP network. Additionally, 3 static IP address are defined for your servers: 10.1.2.31-10.1.2.33. </span><span id=\"ts_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">After a while 20 more IP addresses need to be distributed in the network. It is possible to distribute the </span><span id=\"tt_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">extra IP address without adding another DHCP Server:</span></p>', 1, '', 1, 100.0000000, 0.0000000, 'multichoice', 1, '192.168.19.27+260422071237+oNfaUM', 1776841957, 1776841957, 2, 2),
(58, 0, 'No4', '<p><span id=\"tq_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">You have a DHCP server on your MikroTik router. The IP addresses 10.1.2.2-10.2.2.20 are distributed in </span><span id=\"tr_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">the DHCP network. Additionally, 3 static IP address are defined for your servers: 10.1.2.31-10.1.2.33. </span><span id=\"ts_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">After a while 20 more IP addresses need to be distributed in the network. It is possible to distribute the </span><span id=\"tt_1\" class=\"t s1_1\">extra IP address without adding another DHCP Server:</span></p>', 1, '', 1, 1.0000000, 0.0000000, 'multichoice', 1, '192.168.19.27+260422071641+kEJvrB', 1776842201, 1776842201, 2, 2),
(59, 0, 'No5', '<p>In which order are the entries in Access List and Connect List processed?</p>', 1, '', 1, 100.0000000, 0.0000000, 'multichoice', 1, '192.168.19.27+260422071415+JcnC6H', 1776842055, 1776842055, 2, 2),
